course: dictionary
lesson: 2546
title: What a deficit means
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A deficit is the amount that is missing. If you need 50 and you have 35, the deficit is 15, because 15 is how much is still short. Deficit is a noun, and its plural is deficits.
explain: Money uses deficit too. «The government's budget is its plan for money; a deficit is spending more than it collects, like spending £100 and collecting £90, so it borrows £10.» The shortfall there is £10, so the deficit is £10.
explain: Sport uses it as well. A team that «came back from a two-goal deficit» was two goals behind before it caught up. Look for clues like «a deficit of» or «make up the deficit»: they show that something is short and needs filling.
fact: A deficit is a shortfall: how much is missing compared with what is needed.
fact: In money, a deficit means spending more than the money coming in.
fact: In sport, a deficit is the number of points or goals a team is behind.
fact: «Budget deficit» means a government spends more than it collects in taxes.
fact: «Make up the deficit» means to fill the missing amount.
exercise: You need 50 and you have 35. What is the deficit? | *15 | 85 | 10 | 35
exercise: «The government's budget is its plan for money; a deficit is spending more than it collects, like spending £100 and collecting £90.» What is the deficit here? | £90 | £100 | £190 | *£10
exercise: «The team came back from a two-goal deficit.» What does deficit mean in this sentence? | A prize for winning | *Goals the team was behind | Players who were injured | Goals the team scored in a row
test: «She had a sleep deficit after a week of late nights.» What does sleep deficit suggest? | *She had not had enough sleep | She had lots of spare sleep | She was ill with a cold | She slept too much
test: What does «make up the deficit» mean? | Spend more money | Count the points | Lose the game | *Fill the missing amount
exam: Which sentence uses deficit correctly to mean money spent more than money coming in? | My deficit is my favourite colour | The deficit was my favourite song | *A government has a budget deficit because it spends more than it collects | A team has a deficit of three goals
